-- CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-3 (2026-10-19, pillar autonomy; agent_issues 2826 PATHS-UNTESTED-1 and 2880 controls_on_critical_path_untested, context 100217 CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-RUNNER-1). Third seed
-- of migrations/2026-10-19-control-alternate-probes.sql (and ...probes2.sql), written after the runner landed: PR 3079 (qnfo-fleet-control 0.40.0, chaosDrill reads
-- control_alternate_probes, judges each row with chaosJudge and stamps control_registry.alternate_tested_at only on a pass) merged at 17:38Z, and the drill ran at about 18:00Z.
-- Measured 2026-10-19 18:1xZ, qnfo-audit, SELECT only: v_control_alternate_status drilled 30, no-probe 65 of which 7 untested (v_control_alternate_untested.controls_untested_without_probe 7),
-- not-exercisable 1, probe-failing 2 (cf-obs-nested-too-deep-pin, whose detector fm-trigger-depth-compile does not read pass: a real failure the drill filed as its own
-- CHAOS-DRILL-FAILED-1 issue and outside this file, and control-alternate-probes, which fails on the same 7), removed 3. The detector
-- fm-control-alternate-undrilled reads that figure and fails with it, and v_path_coverage_violations alternate-untested still lists them. The seven controls: model_floor_pr_check,
-- research-model-skip-gauge, research-fallback-price-guard, relapse-reopen-window, verification-deferral-escalation, improvement-loop-relapse-trigger-judge, code-task-publish-patch-cap
-- (the last is on the critical path, critical_untested_by_register 1).
--   * Four of them leave a trace in D1 that a read can observe, and get a read-only expected/observed probe in the shape of the first two files (a state check on the alternate's own
--     objects plus an event inside a window stated in minutes, 120 where the event is continuous): code-task-publish-patch-cap (alternate: a session pull request with no patch cap and the
--     LOOP-BREAKER-1 hand-off of a refused oversize patch), relapse-reopen-window (the D1 trigger remediation_reopen_on_relapse_d1, the view v_closure_relapses and the detector
--     fm-relapse-window-close-anchor), verification-deferral-escalation (the detector fm-verification-deferral-unaged over the same deferred_since column and escalation issue title),
--     improvement-loop-relapse-trigger-judge (the guard metric fix_target_hold_rate_30d and the improvement loop state that keeps it). Nothing is stamped here: the drill stamps a pass.
--   * Three do not: model_floor_pr_check (a GitHub Actions workflow), research-model-skip-gauge (an isolate's memory) and research-fallback-price-guard (a rule over code constants). The
--     second file left them unprobed on the reading that they leave no trace in D1, and this file checked that reading against D1 (SELECT only, 2026-10-19, results in the evidence notes and in
--     blocker_redteam): no table of workflow runs, 0 ai-skip events ever, 0 events for the wait path ever. A probe for them could only pass by absence, which would stamp a declaration, so each carries ALTERNATE-NOT-EXERCISABLE
--     with its reason in control_registry.evidence and alternate_tested_at stays NULL on purpose.
--   * The recorded reason did not clear them: v_path_coverage_gaps (and v_control_alternate_status) excused a row only when its alternate_path started with 'none needed', and these three
--     carry real alternate text. Both clauses now read the marker on a row that has no probe, so a row that later gains a probe is judged by the probe again and a marker never hides
--     a probed row. The two views are replaced by DROP VIEW and CREATE VIEW after their SQL is copied to bak_20261019_path_alt_views (their columns are unchanged, and
--     v_path_coverage_violations and v_control_alternate_untested, the only readers in qnfo-audit, read them by name and are not touched).
-- The session pull request clause of the code-task-publish-patch-cap probe is demand-conditioned, not standing: it fails only while an open LOOP-BREAKER-1 oversize issue filed more than 120
-- minutes ago has no session merge in work_claims after the moment it was filed. A standing "a session merged in the last 1440 minutes" clause would have read false for about 5220 minutes
-- (work_claims read 2026-10-19: the last session merge before that day was 2026-10-14T13:32Z, the next 2026-10-19T04:34Z, so the 1440 minute window was empty from 2026-10-15T13:32Z) and filed a CHAOS-DRILL-FAILED-1 issue at about 14 drills of 360 minutes that only a session merge could close.
-- Live read-only runs 2026-10-19 18:5xZ: the four probes each return expected ok, observed ok against qnfo-audit (the patch-cap probe with its demand-conditioned clause too: the open hand-offs 100184 and 100227 have 55 and 37 session merges after they were filed).
-- Failure mode control-alternate-reason-unread (the register records a reason the views do not read: the defect above) gets its failure_modes row and the fm- detector
-- fm-control-alternate-reason-unread, which compares the register with both views every hour and reads 0 after this file.
-- Repair after review (two blocking findings, both on the three ALTERNATE-NOT-EXERCISABLE reasons):
--   * The widened views clear any probe-less, untested control for the bare token, whatever its alternate_path, and v_blocker_claims scans only agent_issues and human_actions, so a text edit of
--     control_registry.evidence could zero v_path_coverage_violations and controls_untested_without_probe for any future control. The views keep the widened clause (the spec asks for it) and the
--     detector fm-control-alternate-reason-unread now also counts a control with the token, no probe, no tested date and an alternate_path that does not start with none needed (the three
--     CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-1 rows keep their old standing) that has no blocker_redteam row with target control:<name> and verdict confirmed-with-evidence. The three new controls each have one.
--   * The three premises are measurements with a date, not facts: 0 ai-skip events and 0 no-fallback ai-warn events (qnfo-research-exec 0.25.0 shipped on 2026-10-19, the provider limited 1176 calls on
--     2026-10-17, 2956 on 2026-10-18 and one on 2026-10-19), and a green run of the model-floor-guard workflow leaves no D1 record. DOCTRINE-1 puts a belief that is acted on in belief_registry with a
--     belief-<key> probe, so each reason gets one: alt-unexercisable-<control>, probed hourly by the remediation tick (expected ok, observed ok while the premise holds, and a sentence naming the
--     step to take once it breaks). The detector reads v_belief_status too and counts a reason whose belief reads falsified, so a premise that breaks turns fm-control-alternate-reason-unread red
--     within the hour instead of lying in a list that nothing grades. The doer for the one alternate that cannot be observed at all is agent_issues MODEL-FLOOR-GUARD-OBSERVABLE-1 (code-task for
--     qnfo-github-steward, then the probe row that retires the reason), with a closing probe on the issue.
-- Rows written: control_alternate_probes 4 (INSERT OR IGNORE), control_registry evidence on 7 rows (a NOT LIKE guard makes a second apply change nothing), blocker_redteam 3 (one per
-- reason, guarded by target), belief_registry 3 with their 3 belief-<key> contracts, agent_issues 1 (open title is unique) with its contract set, failure_modes 1, remediation_contracts 1 detector,
-- decision_log 1, bak_20261019_path_alt_views 2. Expected effect: controls_untested_without_probe 7 to 0 (the detector turns green at its next hourly run and the control-alternate-probes
-- probe at the next drill), v_path_coverage_violations alternate-untested leaves the three not-exercisable rows at once and the four probed rows when the drill passes them.
